{{- /*
What the tool server says to an agent, one template per kind of answer. Go passes data and no
text. A role, a status or a delivery arrives spelled as its enum is (names.Spell), so a template
branches on the enum's own words.
*/ -}}

{{- define "oneof" -}}
Give exactly one of {{list .Fields}}{{if .Doc}} ({{.Doc}}){{end}}.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "arguments" -}}
The arguments of {{.Tool}} are wrong:
{{range .Problems}}- {{template "problem" .}}
{{end}}Fix them against the tool's input schema and call again.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "problem" -}}
{{- if eq .Kind "unknown" -}}
unknown field `{{.Field}}`: this tool takes only {{.Want}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "type" -}}
`{{.Field}}` must be {{.Want}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "enum" -}}
{{if .Got}}`{{.Field}}` is `{{.Got}}`, which is not one of: {{.Want}}{{else}}`{{.Field}}` must be one of: {{.Want}}{{end}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "required" -}}
`{{.Field}}` is required{{if .Detail}}: {{.Detail}}{{end}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "group" -}}
{{if .Field}}`{{.Field}}`: g{{else}}G{{end}}ive exactly one of {{.Want}}{{if .Doc}} ({{.Doc}}){{end}}
{{- else -}}
{{if .Field}}`{{.Field}}`: {{end}}{{.Detail}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "wrong_role_body" -}}
You are a {{.Role}}, so your handoff goes in the `{{.Role}}` field and in no other, and you gave `{{.Given}}`: call post_handoff again with the `{{.Role}}` field.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "missing_role_body" -}}
Your handoff has no `{{.Role}}` field, which is the body for a {{.Role}}: call post_handoff again with it.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "spawn_agent" -}}
started agent {{.Agent}}. It will post a handoff when it is done; list_agents shows where it stands.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "send_message" -}}
message {{.Message}} is {{if eq .Delivery "steered"}}steered into the agent's running turn
{{- else if eq .Delivery "new_turn"}}starting the agent's next turn
{{- else if eq .Delivery "queued"}}queued until the agent's turn ends
{{- else if eq .Delivery "rejected"}}rejected
{{- else}}on its way{{end}}.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "stop_agent" -}}
agent {{.Agent}} is being stopped.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "post_handoff" -}}
handoff sent to your lead. You are done: end your turn.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "post_report" -}}
report sent to the operator.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "list_agents" -}}
{{- if not .Agents -}}
Your run has no agents.
{{- else -}}
The agents of your run:
{{range .Agents}}- {{.ID}}{{if .Self}} (you){{end}}: {{.Role}}{{if .Plan}}, plan {{.Plan}}{{end}}, {{template "status" .Status}}{{if .Parent}}, started by {{.Parent}}{{end}}
{{end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "status" -}}
{{- if eq . "launching" -}}starting its session
{{- else if eq . "active" -}}working on a turn
{{- else if eq . "waiting" -}}waiting for its subagents
{{- else if eq . "idle" -}}idle, between turns
{{- else if eq . "ended" -}}finished, its session closed
{{- else if eq . "failed" -}}failed
{{- else if eq . "lost" -}}lost, its session went away
{{- else -}}in an unknown state
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "transport_refused" -}}
the orchestrator refused this session ({{.Message}}): stop and tell the operator; do not retry
{{- end -}}

{{- define "transport_rejected" -}}
the orchestrator rejected the request ({{.Message}}): fix the arguments and call again
{{- end -}}

{{- define "transport_unanswered" -}}
the orchestrator did not answer ({{.Message}}): call list_agents to see whether your last call took effect, then repeat it only if it did not
{{- end -}}

{{- define "no_such_tool" -}}
there is no tool `{{.Name}}`: the tools you have are {{.Tools}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "tool_not_for_role" -}}
{{.Name}} is not available to a {{.Role}}: the tools you have are {{.Tools}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "refusal" -}}
{{- if eq .Refusal "run_not_found" -}}
your run does not exist on this orchestrator: stop work and tell the operator
{{- else if eq .Refusal "agent_not_found" -}}
no agent has that id: call list_agents for the ids that exist
{{- else if eq .Refusal "not_permitted" -}}
your role may not do this: post_handoff to the lead instead if you are a subagent
{{- else if eq .Refusal "run_not_running" -}}
the run is stopping or over: finish what you hold, then post your handoff or report
{{- else if eq .Refusal "fanout_limit" -}}
the run already has the most subagents it may have live: wait for a handoff, or stop a subagent with stop_agent, then spawn again
{{- else if eq .Refusal "agent_is_lead" -}}
the lead stops only with its run: ask the operator to stop the run
{{- else if eq .Refusal "agent_not_live" -}}
that agent's session is already over or closing: call list_agents to see which agents are live
{{- else if eq .Refusal "agent_not_allowed" -}}
the operator did not allow that harness and model for this run. It allows only: {{range $i, $a := .Allowed}}{{if $i}}; {{end}}harness {{$a.Harness}} {{if $a.Model}}with model {{$a.Model}}{{else}}with its default model (leave model out){{end}}{{end}}. Spawn again with one of these, or leave the model out to take the first one on the harness; if none fits, tell the operator
{{- else if eq .Refusal "model_not_allowed" -}}
the host does not allow {{if .Model}}the model {{.Model}}{{else}}a model for that agent{{end}}{{if .AllowedModels}}. It allows only: {{range $i, $m := .AllowedModels}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$m}}{{end}}. Spawn again with one of these{{else}}: no model is allowed until the operator fixes the host's settings{{end}}; if none fits, tell the operator
{{- else if eq .Refusal "repository_in_use" -}}
another run is working in this repository: only an operator starts runs, so tell the operator
{{- else if eq .Refusal "time_limit_reached" -}}
the run reached its time limit and starts no new agent: finish with what you have, promote a judged candidate that beats the base if there is one, and post your final report with post_report
{{- else if eq .Refusal "cost_limit_reached" -}}
the run reached its cost limit and starts no new agent: finish with what you have, promote a judged candidate that beats the base if there is one, and post your final report with post_report
{{- else if eq .Refusal "no_viewer" -}}
a catch-up is for the operator's client, which names who is looking: this is not a tool you have, so do not call it
{{- else if eq .Refusal "handoff_not_yours" -}}
your handoff has no body for your role, or has another role's: give it again with the `{{.Role}}` field and no other body
{{- else if or (eq .Refusal "eval_place_not_found") (eq .Refusal "eval_place_misfit") (eq .Refusal "eval_place_ambiguous") -}}
only an operator starts a run or chooses its eval place: this is not a tool you have, so tell the operator
{{- else if or (eq .Refusal "setup_incomplete") (eq .Refusal "not_in_setup") -}}
only an operator completes a setup: this is not a tool you have, so tell the operator what is left to do
{{- else -}}
the orchestrator refused the command: {{.Refusal}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
